WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:05.500
Television is so glamorous... sorry, I
shouldn't have talked.

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:10.400
One of the most persuasive arguments against a universal basic
income is the people will stop working.

00:00:10.969 --> 00:00:14.360
They'll take the universal basic income,
they'll pool it and they will simply

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:16.369
live in idle life.

00:00:16.369 --> 00:00:19.880
It's a serious issue and I had to take
that into account in the design of the

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:24.890
program. And the solution that I came up
with is pretty straightforward. As long

00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:30.230
as people have a job that pays less than
thirty thousand dollars a year, they

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:33.590
continue to get the full ten thousand
dollars.

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:38.149
Now there is a certain tax that is
levied on after thirty thousand dollars

00:00:38.149 --> 00:00:42.800
a year, but at that point you have to ask
yourself are you going to quit work and

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:47.120
exchange a forty thousand dollar a year
lifestyle for a ten-thousand-dollar a year

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:53.239
lifestyle? People to live satisfying
lives need to be responsible for their

00:00:53.239 --> 00:00:54.469
own lives.

00:00:54.469 --> 00:00:58.280
There's much more to be said about the
problem of work disincentives, but a

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:03.230
program of a universal basic income can
be structured so the people are lured

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:06.230
into working until they can't afford to
quit.

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:08.750
 

